[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Caro-Kann: Two Knights Attack"]
[Variation "Two Knights, 3...Bg4"]
[ECO "B11"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "pin"]
[Themes "quick-development,question-the-bishop"]

1. e4 c6 2. Nc3 { Prepares d4 and keeps e4 defended without committing the d-pawn. } 2... d5
3. Nf3 { Develops, and covers e5 and d4 so Black's centre has nothing to hit. } 3... Bg4
{ Black pins the knight against the queen and eyes d5 and f3. }
4. h3 { Asks the bishop to decide now, before Black builds the pin. } 4... Bxf3
( 4... Bh5 5. exd5 { Takes while the bishop is stuck on h5. } 5... cxd5 6. Bb5+ { Check: the knight on c6 must block. } 6... Nc6 7. g4 { The pawn push traps the bishop's retreat. } )
5. Qxf3 { The queen is safe here and White keeps the bishop pair. } 5... e6
6. d4 { Takes the centre now the bishop is gone. } 6... Nf6 7. Bd3 { Develops towards the kingside and keeps an eye on h7. } 7... dxe4 8. Nxe4 { Recaptures with the knight and keeps the centre. } 8... Nxe4 9. Bxe4 { The bishop is well placed, pointing at the kingside. } 9... Nd7 *
